# Rocketship overview

## What it is

- A themeable, CSS-first component library: Astro in `packages/base` (`@labcat2020/rocketship`), Svelte ports in `packages/svelte` (`@labcat2020/rocketship-svelte`).
- A pnpm monorepo: library packages in `packages/*`, Storybook hosts in `apps/*` (`apps/frontend` for Astro, `apps/svelte` for Svelte). The apps are not products.
- Every package is published to npm; the apps use them through workspace references.
- Later: add-on packages (forms, layout, ecommerce) that extend the base without breaking it, Payload templates and a Figma kit.

## Principles

- CSS and SCSS before JavaScript. The MVP is complete with CSS-only components and themes before any JS-required component is added.
- Components are styled through `--rs-*` custom properties with token defaults.
- BEM with the `rs` prefix for every block.

## Where things are

- Vision, decisions and roadmap: `_planning/rocketship-plan.md`. Tasks and acceptance criteria: `_planning/tasks.md`.
- Why each component rule exists: `_planning/component-review-decisions.md`.
- Tokens and themes: `rocketship-themes.mdc`.
- Building a component: `.agents/skills/rocketship-component/SKILL.md` (Astro) or `.agents/skills/rocketship-component-svelte/SKILL.md` (Svelte).
- Stories: `rocketship-stories.mdc`. Run Storybook with `pnpm storybook` (Astro) or `pnpm storybook:svelte` from the repo root.
